cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these editions, please cite the specific release you have used, as below."
type: dataset
title: "The Gothic Bible: LegOst Digital Editions"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-14
abstract: >-
  TEI-encoded diplomatic-interpretative digital editions of the witnesses to
  the Gothic Bible, produced within the PRIN 2022 project LegOst (The Textual
  Legacy of the Ostrogoths in Italy: The Gothic Bible and Other Texts) and
  published on Archivum Gothicum. Volume 1 comprises the Codex Argenteus with
  the Speyer fragment, the Codex Carolinus, the Codex Gissensis, and the
  Ambrosiani C and D. The repository also contains the encoding documentation,
  the Word-to-TEI conversion scripts and the customisations made to EVT 3.
